# DIRECT dependencies only -- the ones api/ actually asks for. Edit THIS file.
#
# `requirements.txt` next to it is a LOCK: every package, transitives included,
# pinned to the exact version verified running in the container. The Dockerfile
# installs the lock, never this file. Regenerate with:
#
#     bash scripts/lock-requirements.sh
#
# Why a lock at all: nothing here used to be pinned, so each rebuild re-resolved
# the whole tree from scratch. On 2026-09-17 that resolved `anthropic` and `mcp`
# to versions requiring **httpx2** instead of httpx, the transitive httpx that
# auth.py imports by name disappeared, main.py died at import, and every route
# 502'd. An unpinned requirements file means the image you build today is not the
# image you built last week, and nothing tells you which dependency moved.

fastapi
uvicorn
starlette
pydantic

# Without this, uvicorn --reload silently falls back to StatReload, which POLLS:
# it rglob()s every reload dir for *.py every 0.25s and stats each hit. Installed,
# uvicorn picks WatchFilesReload instead (inotify -- event-driven, ~0% idle CPU),
# and --reload-include/--reload-exclude start working at all. Not optional here:
# the poller was burning 44% of a core around the clock on a 2-core box.
watchfiles

# Imported by name in auth.py. Do not assume anthropic or mcp still drag it in --
# that assumption is exactly what caused the 2026-09-17 outage.
httpx

anthropic
mcp
discord.py

google-api-python-client
google-auth-httplib2
google-auth-oauthlib

pillow
reportlab
pymupdf
python-multipart
icalendar
websockets
